# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 231-236 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 17 — CHAPTERS 22-25, LEAN, 2026-09-25): the ox and the ass side by side, every pair of kinds,
# the man and the ass, threshing and driving, the mule and the tied horse (231); the mingled stuff combed, spun and woven — the acronym, the covering and the
# pack, the shirt over the shirt, the strip and the strap, the felts (232); THE ONE UTTERANCE five times — the tassels against the mingled stuff, remember and
# keep (233:1 REREAD WHOLE from chapter 5), the Sabbath's death and its lambs, the brother's wife and the levirate, the daughter's inheritance (233); the tassels'
# threads by the two schools, the four corners, not from the made, the cloaks that are not square, the pillow and the sheet, the smock (234); the hated bride —
# R. Judah's lashes, the light and the weighty, the charge by the analogy, in her presence, the witnesses, the father's door, the father and mother disgraced,
# the woman's silence, the minor betrothed (235); the tokens as refuting witnesses, the plaintiff first, the levirate widow (236 — HEADLESS inside 22:16-17).
# Every row READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by ch22_ink.SP_. Sitting 16's form.
from ch22_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(231, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"PLOW NOT WITH AN OX AND AN ASS TOGETHER" (22:10) — FOREVER? "THAT YOUR OX AND YOUR ASS MAY REST" (Exodus 23:12) — THEY ALREADY WORK; SO "TOGETHER" — THIS ONE WITH THAT ONE; ONLY OX AND ASS? EVERY BEAST, ANIMAL AND BIRD FROM "PLOW NOT"; WHY "OX AND ASS"? WITH AN OX AND AN ASS YOU MAY NOT, BUT WITH A MAN AND AN ASS YOU MAY. The head row of piska 231 ({SP_(231, 1, "זה", "עם", "זה")} "this one with that one"; {SP_(231, 1, "באדם", "ובחמור")} "with a man and with an ass"): THE PAIR\'S LAW — every two kinds (Kilayim 8:2), the man excluded from the pair (Kilayim 8:6); the Sabbath verse the ground that the beasts work. Fresh.')
srow(231, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"PLOW NOT" — ONLY PLOWING? THRESHING, SITTING AND DRIVING FROM "TOGETHER" — ANYWHERE; R. MEIR EXEMPTS THE SITTER. ({SP_(231, 2, "הדש", "והיושב", "והמנהיג")} "the thresher, the sitter and the driver"; {SP_(231, 2, "רבי", "מאיר", "פוטר", "ביושב")} "R. Meir exempts the sitter"): every labor of the pair — the sitter in the wagon a DISPUTED cell. Fresh.')
srow(231, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"TOGETHER" — EXCLUDING THE MULE; "TOGETHER" — EXCLUDING ONE WHO TIES A HORSE TO THE WAGON\'S SIDE OR BEHIND IT, AND THE LIBYAN ASS WITH CAMELS. ({SP_(231, 3, "פרט", "לרמך")} "excluding the mule"; {SP_(231, 3, "לצדי", "הקרון")} "to the sides of the wagon"): the mule one beast, the tied horse not yoked — the pair\'s definition (Kilayim 8:4). Fresh.')
srow(232, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WEAR NOT MINGLED STUFF" (22:11) — NOT SHORN WOOL AND LINEN SHREDS? "SHAATNEZ" (the mingled stuff) — A THING COMBED, SPUN AND WOVEN; R. SHIMON B. ELAZAR SAYS: HE IS TWISTED AND TWISTS HIS FATHER IN HEAVEN AGAINST HIMSELF. The head row of piska 232 ({SP_(232, 1, "דבר", "ששוע", "טווי", "ונוז")} "a thing combed, spun and woven"): THE WORD READ BY NOTARIKON (the acronym reading) — shaatnez as shua-tavui-nuz, the three operations the definition (Kilayim 9:8, Sifra Kedoshim); the compile\'s predicate on the fabric. Fresh.')
srow(232, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"WEAR NOT" — ONLY WEARING? COVERING FROM "IT SHALL NOT COME UPON YOU" (Leviticus 19:19); A PACK ON HIS BACK? "WEAR NOT" — WEARING WAS IN THE CLASS AND WAS SINGLED OUT TO COMPARE: AS WEARING BENEFITS THE BODY, SO ALL THAT BENEFITS THE BODY. ({SP_(232, 2, "שהיא", "הנית", "הגוף")} "which is a benefit of the body"): the act\'s class by the prototype — bodily benefit, not carrying (I3). Fresh.')
srow(232, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"TOGETHER" — A WOOL SHIRT OVER A LINEN SHIRT, A LINEN OVER A WOOL? "TOGETHER". ({SP_(232, 3, "חלוק", "של", "צמר", "על", "גבי", "חלוק", "של", "פשתן")} "a shirt of wool over a shirt of linen"): two garments no mixture — one fabric the condition. Fresh.')
srow(232, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'R. HANANIAH B. GAMLIEL SAYS: WHENCE THAT ONE MAY NOT KNOT A WOOL STRIP TO A LINEN ONE TO GIRD HIS LOINS, EVEN WITH A STRAP BETWEEN? "TOGETHER" — ANYWHERE; SO THE SACK AND THE BASKET COMBINE INTO MIXED STUFF. ({SP_(232, 4, "אף", "על", "פי", "שהרצועה", "באמצע")} "even though the strap is between"; {SP_(232, 4, "השק", "והקפה", "מצרפים")} "the sack and the basket combine"): the joining a mixture even through a third material (Kilayim 9:10). Fresh.')
srow(232, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"WOOL AND LINEN TOGETHER" — BUT EACH ALONE IS PERMITTED; THE FELTS ARE FORBIDDEN AS MIXED STUFF — NO WEAVING IN THEM, BUT COMBING. ({SP_(232, 5, "הלבדים", "אסורים", "משום", "כלאים")} "the felts are forbidden as mixed stuff"): one of the three operations enough — combing alone binds the felt (Kilayim 9:9). Fresh.')
srow(233, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WEAR NOT MINGLED STUFF … TASSELS MAKE FOR YOURSELF" (22:11-12) — BOTH WERE SAID IN ONE UTTERANCE; "REMEMBER" (Exodus 20:8) AND "KEEP" (5:12) — BOTH IN ONE UTTERANCE. The head row of piska 233, the second on 22:11 ({SP_(233, 1, "שניהם", "נאמרו", "בדבור", "אחד")} "both were said in one utterance"): THE ONE UTTERANCE — the tassels of wool on a linen garment permitted against the mingled stuff because the two were spoken as one (the exception born with the rule; Menachot 4:1\'s ground), and the Sabbath\'s two words the paradigm — the piska\'s five pairs a LIST OF EXCEPTIONS SPOKEN WITH THEIR RULES: the compile\'s permission edge (tassels -> mingled stuff). REREAD WHOLE (chapter 5, deu_05_vaetchanan).')
srow(233, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"ITS PROFANERS SHALL SURELY DIE" (Exodus 31:14) AND "ON THE SABBATH DAY TWO YEARLING LAMBS" (Numbers 28:9) — BOTH IN ONE UTTERANCE. ({SP_(233, 2, "שניהם", "נאמרו", "בדבור", "אחד")} "both were said in one utterance"): the Sabbath\'s offering slaughtered on the Sabbath — the second exception spoken with its rule. Fresh.')
srow(233, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE NAKEDNESS OF YOUR BROTHER\'S WIFE YOU SHALL NOT UNCOVER" (Leviticus 18:16) AND "HER HUSBAND\'S BROTHER SHALL GO IN TO HER" (25:5) — BOTH IN ONE UTTERANCE. ({SP_(233, 3, "שניהם", "נאמרו", "בדבור", "אחד")} "both were said in one utterance"): THE LEVIRATE AS THE EXCEPTION to the brother\'s wife — 25:5 cited inside chapter 22\'s spine (this row sat among chapter 25\'s outside set at the dump); the third pair. Fresh.')
srow(233, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"EVERY DAUGHTER INHERITING AN INHERITANCE" (Numbers 36:8) AND "THE INHERITANCE SHALL NOT TURN FROM TRIBE TO TRIBE" (Numbers 36:9) — BOTH IN ONE UTTERANCE. ({SP_(233, 4, "שניהם", "נאמרו", "בדבור", "אחד")} "both were said in one utterance"): the heiress\'s marriage inside her tribe with the inheritance\'s fixity — the fourth pair (Zelophehad\'s daughters on the tape). Fresh.')
srow(233, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'WHAT FLESH AND BLOOD CANNOT — TO SAY TWO THINGS AS ONE — AS "GOD SPOKE ONCE; TWO HAVE I HEARD" (Psalm 62:12). ({SP_(233, 5, "אחת", "דבר", "אלהים", "שתים", "זו", "שמענו")} "God spoke once; two have I heard"): the ground of the one utterance — the divine speech\'s form; the translator notes the whole piska thinly attested before the Tosafists. Fresh.')
srow(234, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"TASSELS MAKE FOR YOURSELF" (22:12) — WHY SAID, WHEN "THEY SHALL MAKE THEM FRINGES" (Numbers 15:38) IS SAID? MIGHT ONE MAKE A SINGLE THREAD ALONE? "TASSELS". The head row of piska 234 ({SP_(234, 1, "יעשה", "חוט", "אחד", "בפני", "עצמו")} "make one thread alone"): the plural "tassels" against the single thread — the count\'s floor. Fresh.')
srow(234, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'HOW MANY TASSELS ARE MADE? NOT LESS THAN THREE THREADS, AS THE SCHOOL OF HILLEL; THE SCHOOL OF SHAMMAI SAYS: FOUR THREADS OF BLUE AND FOUR OF WHITE, FOUR FINGERS EACH. ({SP_(234, 2, "אין", "פחות", "משלשה", "חוטים")} "not less than three threads"; {SP_(234, 2, "מארבעה", "חוטים", "של", "תכלת")} "from four threads of blue"): THE TASSELS\' PARAMETERS — three or four threads, four fingers — the two schools\' numbers. Fresh.')
srow(234, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'AND THE LAW IS AS THE SCHOOL OF SHAMMAI; WHEN? AT THE START; BUT ITS REMNANTS AND SHREDS — ANY LENGTH. ({SP_(234, 3, "והלכה", "כדברי", "בית", "שמיי")} "and the law is as the words of the school of Shammai"): SHAMMAI\'S RULING STANDS — a rare verdict for that school (Menachot 41b the Talmud\'s discussion, not opened); the length at making only. Fresh.')
srow(234, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"ON FOUR" — EXCLUDING GARMENTS OF THREE, FIVE, SIX, SEVEN AND EIGHT CORNERS; ANOTHER WORD: "TASSELS MAKE" — THE WHITE; WHENCE THE BLUE? "THEY SHALL PUT ON THE FRINGE OF THE CORNER A THREAD OF BLUE" (Numbers 15:38). ({SP_(234, 4, "יצאו", "בעלי", "שלשה")} "those of three are excluded"; {SP_(234, 4, "זה", "לבן")} "this is the white"): the four corners exact, and Deuteronomy\'s white with Numbers\' blue — the two verses one commandment (Sifrei Numbers 115). Fresh.')
srow(234, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"MAKE" — AND NOT FROM THE MADE: NOT DRAWING LOOSE THREADS FROM THE CLOAK; "ON FOUR" — AND NOT ON EIGHT; "YOUR COVERING" — EXCLUDING THE TOGA AND THE OTHER CLOAKS, NOT BEING SQUARE; R. ELIEZER B. JACOB SAYS: NOT IN THE GARMENT\'S MIDDLE BUT ON ITS EDGE — "ON FOUR CORNERS". ({SP_(234, 5, "ולא", "מן", "העשוי")} "and not from the made"; {SP_(234, 5, "לפי", "שאינם", "מרבעים")} "because they are not square"): the making\'s form — new threads, the square garment, the corner\'s edge (Kilayim 9:6\'s list of cloaks). Fresh.')
srow(234, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR COVERING" — EXCLUDING THE PILLOW; "YOUR COVERING" — EXCLUDING THE SHEET; "YOU COVER" — EXCLUDING THE SOLDIER\'S BLANKET. ({SP_(234, 6, "פרט", "לכר")} "excluding the pillow"; {SP_(234, 6, "פרט", "לסגוס")} "excluding the soldier\'s blanket"): the garment worn, not the bedding (the English cites "Dt.11:12" — the translator\'s slip for 22:12). Fresh.')
srow(234, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"WITH IT" — EXCLUDING A SMOCK THAT DOES NOT COVER HIS HEAD AND MOST OF HIM. ({SP_(234, 7, "פרט", "למעפורת")} "excluding the smock"): THE GARMENT\'S SIZE PARAMETER — the head and most of the body. Fresh.')
srow(235, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN A MAN TAKES A WIFE AND GOES IN TO HER AND HATES HER" (22:13) — R. JUDAH SAYS: IF HE WENT IN TO HER — HE IS FLOGGED; IF NOT — NOT. The head row of piska 235 ({SP_(235, 1, "אם", "בא", "עליה", "לוקה")} "if he went in to her — he is flogged"): the intercourse a CONDITION of the slanderer\'s penalty (R. Judah; 236:2 again) — the compile\'s condition on the bride\'s case. Fresh.')
srow(235, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND HATES HER" — HENCE: ONE WHO TRANSGRESSES A LIGHT COMMANDMENT WILL TRANSGRESS A WEIGHTY ONE: "LOVE YOUR NEIGHBOR" (Leviticus 19:18), THEN "TAKE NO VENGEANCE", THEN "HATE NOT YOUR BROTHER IN YOUR HEART" (19:17), THEN "THAT YOUR BROTHER MAY LIVE WITH YOU" (25:36) — UNTIL HE COMES TO BLOODSHED. ({SP_(235, 2, "עבר", "אדם", "על", "מצוה", "קלה")} "a man transgressed a light commandment"; {SP_(235, 2, "לידי", "שפיכות", "דמים")} "to bloodshed"): the homily of the hater\'s descent — no rule. Fresh.')
srow(235, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND LAYS A CHARGE OF WORDS" (22:14) — EVEN "YOU BURNED THE DISH" WHEN SHE DID NOT? "A CHARGE OF WORDS" HERE AND "A CHARGE OF WORDS" (22:17) — A VERBAL ANALOGY: AS THERE A CLAIM ON THE TOKENS, SO HERE; OR AS THERE THE PLACE OF THE TOKENS, SO HERE — WHENCE ANOTHER MANNER OF INTERCOURSE? "AND BROUGHT ON HER AN EVIL NAME". ({SP_(235, 3, "לגזרה", "שוה")} "for a verbal analogy"; {SP_(235, 3, "טענת", "בתולים")} "a claim on the tokens"): THE ANALOGY INSIDE THE CHAPTER (I2 — 22:14 with 22:17): the charge is a claim of unchastity, not any complaint; the compile\'s predicate on the charge. Fresh.')
srow(235, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SAYS: THIS WOMAN" — HE SPEAKS HIS WORDS ONLY IN HER PRESENCE. ({SP_(235, 4, "אלא", "בעמידתה")} "only when she stands"): the charge before the accused — a procedure parameter. Fresh.')
srow(235, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"I TOOK, CAME NEAR TO HER AND FOUND NO TOKENS" — HERE ARE WITNESSES THAT SHE PLAYED THE HARLOT IN HER FATHER\'S HOUSE. ({SP_(235, 5, "הרי", "עדים", "שזינתה", "בבית", "אביה")} "here are witnesses that she fornicated in her father\'s house"): THE CHARGE IS WITNESSES — the husband\'s claim carried by witnesses of her unchastity while betrothed (Ketubot 4:3\'s case), not the cloth alone; the compile\'s evidence parameter. Fresh.')
srow(235, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN A MAN TAKES A WIFE" — WHY SAID? "A MAN WHO COMMITS ADULTERY WITH A MAN\'S WIFE" (Leviticus 20:10) — WITNESSES IN HER HUSBAND\'S HOUSE THAT SHE SINNED IN HER FATHER\'S, OR IN HER FATHER\'S HOUSE THAT SHE SINNED THERE — JUDGED AT THE CITY GATE? THE VERSE TAKES OUT THE FIRST: SHE IS JUDGED AT HER FATHER\'S DOOR. ({SP_(235, 6, "על", "פתח", "בית", "אביה")} "at the door of her father\'s house"): THE PLACE OF EXECUTION by the witnesses\' timing — the father\'s door for the bride (22:21), the gate for the betrothed girl (22:24); two arms of one status. Fresh.')
srow(235, 7, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND HATES HER" — R. ISHMAEL SAYS: COME AND SEE WHAT HATRED CAUSES — IT BRINGS TO EVIL SPEECH. ({SP_(235, 7, "לידי", "לשון", "הרע")} "to evil speech"): the second homily on the hater; a row citing nothing in either file. Fresh.')
srow(235, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE FATHER OF THE GIRL AND HER MOTHER TAKE" (22:15) — ONLY WITH A FATHER AND A MOTHER? A FATHER WITHOUT A MOTHER, A MOTHER WITHOUT A FATHER, NEITHER — "THE GIRL" ANYWHERE; WHY "FATHER AND MOTHER"? THEY WHO RAISED BAD OFFSPRING COME AND ARE DISGRACED WITH THEM. ({SP_(235, 8, "לא", "אב", "ולא", "אם", "מנין")} "neither father nor mother — whence?"; {SP_(235, 8, "שגדלו", "גדולים", "רעים")} "who raised bad offspring"): the orphan bride inside the law; THE SPINE WRITES "THE GIRL" IN FULL where the Torah writes her as a boy (the ink\'s find 13 — the citation carries the read form). Fresh.')
srow(235, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND BRING OUT THE GIRL\'S TOKENS" — AS IT SOUNDS. ({SP_(235, 9, "כמשמעו")} "as it sounds"): the tokens literal — the cloth (237 the fuller treatment). Fresh.')
srow(235, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE FATHER OF THE GIRL SAYS TO THE ELDERS" (22:16) — HENCE A WOMAN HAS NO STANDING TO SPEAK IN A MAN\'S PLACE. ({SP_(235, 10, "שאין", "רשות", "לאשה", "לדבר", "במקום", "האיש")} "that a woman has no standing to speak in the man\'s place"): the father the speaker, not the mother — a procedure parameter. Fresh.')
srow(235, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"MY DAUGHTER I GAVE TO THIS MAN" — THE FATHER HAS THE RIGHT TO BETROTH HIS MINOR DAUGHTER. ({SP_(235, 11, "לקדש", "את", "בתו", "קטנה")} "to betroth his minor daughter"): THE FATHER\'S RIGHT over the minor — a status of the family daemon (Kiddushin 2:1 the answer sheet). Fresh.')
srow(236, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO WIFE, AND HE HATES HER; AND HE LAYS A CHARGE OF WORDS, SAYING: I FOUND NO TOKENS IN YOUR DAUGHTER — AND THESE ARE MY DAUGHTER\'S TOKENS" (22:16-17) — HERE ARE WITNESSES TO REFUTE HIS WITNESSES. The head row of the headless piska 236 ({SP_(236, 1, "הרי", "עדים", "להזים", "עדיו", "של", "זה")} "here are witnesses to refute this one\'s witnesses"): THE TOKENS ARE COUNTER-WITNESSES — the plotting witnesses\' law (19:18-19) inside the bride\'s case: the father\'s "tokens" refute the husband\'s witnesses, and 22:18-19\'s penalty is the plotter\'s; the compile\'s CALL on the false-witness cell. Fresh.')
srow(236, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JUDAH SAYS: HE IS NEVER LIABLE UNLESS HE HAD INTERCOURSE. ({SP_(236, 2, "אלא", "אם", "כן", "בעל")} "unless he had intercourse"): 235:1\'s condition repeated for the fine — R. Judah\'s arm. Fresh.')
srow(236, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE FATHER OF THE GIRL SAYS" — THE PLAINTIFF OPENS THE PLEADING FIRST. ({SP_(236, 3, "שתובע", "מתחיל", "בדברים", "תחלה")} "that the plaintiff begins the words first"): COURT ORDER — the claimant speaks first (Bava Kamma 46b the Talmud\'s rule "the claimant opens", not opened); a procedure parameter. Fresh.')
srow(236, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"MARRIED TO A HUSBAND" (22:22) — R. ISHMAEL SAYS: THE VERSE TEACHES ON THE LEVIRATE WIDOW THAT ONE WHO LIES WITH HER IS NOT LIABLE UNTIL SHE IS BEDDED. ({SP_(236, 4, "על", "היבמה")} "on the levirate widow"; {SP_(236, 4, "עד", "שתבעל")} "until she is bedded"): 22:22 read inside piska 236 for the yevamah (the widow awaiting her husband\'s brother) — her status "married" begins at the levir\'s act; the adultery cell\'s condition on 25:5\'s status ahead. Fresh.')
